export (ByteView)

-- A `ByteView` is a run of bytes that can be read and not written: it has
-- `Index`, `Length` and `Iterator`, and no `SetIndex`. Nothing here gives
-- back the storage it reads.
--
-- `String.view(s)` views a string's bytes and `Array.view(xs)` an array's,
-- neither by copying. A string is never written, so a view of one never
-- changes. An array can be, by whoever holds it, and a view of it shows each
-- write as it happens: the view is read-only, not frozen.

import Prelude ()
import Turkey.Bytes (ByteView)
